      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Second-half fade",
          "heading": "Jake White questions fitness, cohesion and confidence after second-half fade against Ireland",
          "body": "Fiji head coach Jake White has raised several questions after the 43-15 loss to Ireland, chiefly why the side keeps fading after the break. Ireland scored 26 unanswered second-half points, and White said Fiji had again leaked tries in the final 20 minutes. \"Is that fitness? Is that time together? Is it cohesion?\" he asked. Fitness, cohesion and confidence in the game plan are all to be discussed before Round 6 against Italy, with decision-making under pressure also on the list."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash. South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
      ]
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Team news",
          "heading": "Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson return from injury for All Blacks clash",
          "body": "England head coach Steve Borthwick has three key men available before Saturday's clash with New Zealand. George Furbank, Ollie Chessum and Seb Atkinson were all named in the 36-man squad on Sunday, after sitting out the 78-15 win over Japan. Chessum, the vice-captain, had a shoulder problem and Atkinson a groin complaint, while Furbank, who shone in his first England appearance in two years against Australia, had a groin problem. Tighthead prop Joe Heyes said: \"We'd expect the best of New Zealand every time we face them.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
      ],
