        "name": "Rugbyrama"
      }
    },
    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Scrum progress",
          "heading": "Kelleher says Ireland's scrum is improving before Springboks test",
          "body": "Ireland's scrum was the one consistent element of the 43-15 win over Fiji, earning four penalties, and Kelleher believes the work is paying off. Recalling last year's 24-13 Aviva defeat, when the Springboks drew six scrum penalties, he said \"It was a very tough day\" and that the scrum pain has at times driven the front row on. There has been no drastic overhaul, just small tweaks, Kelleher added. Ahead of Saturday's Test he hopes they'll have \"enough in the tank\" to do the job."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash. South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
