      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Defensive record",
          "heading": "Jamie Roberts hails Wales' 346-tackle defence after Cardiff win over New Zealand",
          "body": "Former British and Irish Lions centre Jamie Roberts, who won 94 caps for Wales, told BBC Radio 5 Live that the defence in the 35-28 win over New Zealand showed what it means to be Welsh: \"That defensive set in the second half epitomised in a way what it is to be Welsh.\" The numbers back him up. BBC Sport reports Wales made 346 tackles, a Test record, with lock Dafydd Jenkins on 38 and Jac Morgan on 31. Roberts never managed to beat New Zealand during his own Wales career."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash",
          "body": "South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "France squad",
          "heading": "France recall Jalibert and Jelonch, Avogadro included, for Pumas test",
          "body": "France have named 42 players to prepare for the Pumas, with fly-half Matthieu Jalibert back after a quadriceps injury. Flanker Anthony Jelonch returns from concussion, though whether he is used against Argentina is open, and UBB winger Hugo Avogadro joins the senior camp at Marcoussis. Toulouse's Julien Marchand is out for the rest of the Nations Championship with a thigh problem. The Pumas, who beat Italy 19-14 in Genoa, face them on Saturday at the Stade de France."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash. South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
