      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach reaction",
          "heading": "Les Kiss calls Murrayfield loss 'turgid' as Wallabies drop fourth straight Test",
          "body": "Kiss's own description of the match, played in heavy rain, says plenty about the afternoon. Australia had little to show for the effort beyond Max Jorgensen's late try, and the numbers back that up: four straight defeats, and at least 40 points conceded in three Tests running before Murrayfield, the most recent a 45-22 loss to England at Twickenham."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash. South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
      ],
