    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match fallout",
          "heading": "Eddie Jones owns crushing 15-78 England defeat after Hockings red card",
          "body": "Japan head coach Eddie Jones said in his post-match interview, \"I take full responsibility for the result,\" after the 15-78 loss to England. Japan conceded 13 tries, and the damage began in the first minute, when lock Hockings was shown a yellow card for a dangerous tackle, later upgraded to red. England then ran in five tries in about 20 minutes. Japan still scored 15 points, 10 in the first half and 5 in the second."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wales beat New Zealand 35-28, ending long wait for a win",
          "body": "England recall Furbank, Chessum and Atkinson for All Blacks clash. South Africa's Jesse Kriel signs on in Japan."
        }
      ]
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-16",
      "edition": "Monday 16 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Post-match jibe",
          "heading": "Ben Kay recalls Twickenham box asking if All Blacks had been hacked",
          "body": "England great Ben Kay, speaking on TNT Sports, said someone in his Twickenham box asked \"have New Zealand been hacked?\" during Saturday's game in Cardiff. Kay said he and Danny Care had expected a Welsh start followed by a New Zealand response, but \"they just never showed up\". Wales won 35-28, ending 73 years without beating New Zealand, and Kay called them \"absolutely phenomenal\"."
        },
        {
